artifact.self_contained_problem:
An Engel structure on a smooth 4-manifold $M$ is a maximally non-integrable rank-2 distribution $\mathcal{D} \subset TM$; that is, $\mathcal{E} := [\mathcal{D},\mathcal{D}]$ is a rank-3 distribution (an even-contact structure) and $[\mathcal{E},\mathcal{E}] = TM$.

Let $M$ be a smooth 4-manifold equipped with:
(i) a codimension-1 foliation $\mathcal{F}$ (so $T\mathcal{F} \subset TM$ is an integrable rank-3 distribution);
(ii) a rank-2 plane field $\xi \subset T\mathcal{F}$ which is a leafwise contact structure, i.e. for each leaf $L$ of $\mathcal{F}$, $\xi|_L$ is a contact structure on the 3-manifold $L$;
(iii) a splitting $\xi = \ell_1 \oplus \ell_2$ of $\xi$ as a direct sum of two (continuous) line fields on $M$.

Question: Does there always exist a $C^0$-small (equivalently, arbitrarily small) perturbation of the distribution $\xi$ to a rank-2 distribution $\mathcal{D} \subset TM$ that is an Engel structure on $M$?

